  "id": "spc",
  "term": "SPC",
  "definition": "SPC is a heuristic model that distinguishes three kinds of phenomena in psychiatry and psychotherapy: stable mental structures, changeable problems or problem behaviors, and temporary conditions. It is used to clarify what is relatively fixed, what can be worked on or changed, and what is a transient state that must be treated or endured.",
